\newlabel{fig:intent_divergence}{{2}{3}{\textbf  {(a)} Example of intent divergence between EDA sessions using full data \textbf  {(a.1)} vs. using samples \textbf  {(a.2)}. Bad sample selection in (a.2) led to large errors in the result \textit  {R2}. Consequently, user diverted from ideal query sequence and finally found misleading insight in \textit  {R4}. \textbf  {(b)} Workflow of our RL-based {\sc  {approxEDA }}is shown. The agent transparently interacts with a live EDA session (e.g. one on the left) and chooses the best action $a_t$, i.e. the optimal sample to use for the current so that intent divergence is minimized. {\sc  {approxEDA }}'s \textit  {State Space Encoder} combines 4 different information into a state $s_t$ that is used by the policy-network ($\pi _{\theta }$) to decide the best action. }{}{}}
